text: <|channel|>analysis<|message|>We need to answer: difference between stack and queue. Provide explanation: stack LIFO, queue FIFO, operations push/pop vs enqueue/dequeue, usage examples. Provide differences in data structure, operations, applications. Also mention underlying implementations. Provide maybe differences in memory usage, concurrency. Provide typical use cases: stack for recursion, undo, etc; queue for scheduling, BFS, etc. Also mention that stack is like a stack of plates, queue like line at a bank. Provide difference in operations: stack has push/pop, queue has enqueue/dequeue. Also mention that stack can be implemented with array or linked list, queue can be implemented with array or linked list, but queue often uses circular buffer. Provide difference in complexity: both O(1). Provide difference in usage: stack is LIFO, queue is FIFO. Provide difference in typical operations: top vs front. Provide difference in typical data structure: stack uses last in first out, queue uses first in first out. Provide
